{"causes": ["The collapse of Egypt's Middle Kingdom created a power vacuum, enabling the rise of numerous regional rulers like Nebdjefara in the Nile Delta.", "The gradual infiltration and settlement of Canaanite populations in the eastern Delta led to the formation of distinct political entities, including the Fourteenth Dynasty.", "The administrative decentralization following the decline of the Thirteenth Dynasty allowed local potentates to declare independent kingship, even for short durations."], "effects": ["Nebdjefara's brief reign contributed to the political fragmentation characteristic of Egypt's Second Intermediate Period.", "His inclusion in the Turin King List provides modern historians with rare, albeit fragmentary, evidence of the numerous minor pharaohs in the Delta during the 17th century BCE.", "The ephemeral nature of his rule foreshadowed the eventual consolidation of power by the Hyksos in the eastern Nile Delta."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "fourteenth-dynasty-of-egypt", "sourceName": "Fourteenth Dynasty of Egypt", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "nebdjefara", "targetName": "Nebdjefara", "context": "Nebdjefara was a pharaoh who belonged to the Fourteenth Dynasty of Egypt, a group of rulers active during the Second Intermediate Period."}, {"sourceSlug": "second-intermediate-period-of-egypt", "sourceName": "Second Intermediate Period of Egypt", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "nebdjefara", "targetName": "Nebdjefara", "context": "Nebdjefara's brief reign took place entirely within the politically turbulent Second Intermediate Period of Egypt, circa 17th century BCE."}, {"sourceSlug": "turin-king-list", "sourceName": "Turin King List", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "nebdjefara", "targetName": "Nebdjefara", "context": "The Turin King List is the primary ancient source transmitting the name and approximate reign length of Nebdjefara to modern historians."}, {"sourceSlug": "nebdjefara", "sourceName": "Nebdjefara", "verb": "OCCURS_